1. The project is a one-pager built with React + Tailwind CSS.

2. The site presents a construction project: a parking garage named “Autogyron 3,” being developed by Örebro Parkering AB in Örebro, Sweden.

3. Color palette:
   - #c99442 – mustard yellow / orange
   - #5b6a49 – dark green
   - #9e998c – light gray-brown
   - #738c7b – green-gray
   - #dbc3a8 – beige / sand
   These colors should be used for backgrounds, sections, text, buttons, and accents.

4. The hero section at the top must contain two full-width images that auto-slide every 5 seconds with a fade transition.

5. The page must be fully responsive – layout and typography should adapt to both desktop and mobile.

6. The project description must include this text:
   “Örebro Parkering AB intends to build a new parking garage with a total of 250 spaces, consisting of 246 standard spaces and 4 accessible spaces. The building will be located on the Autogyron 3 property in Södra Ladugårdsängen, Örebro. The ground floor will also include a commercial unit built to basic finish, with plumbing preparations for an accessible restroom (RWC) and a small kitchenette.”

7. The UI/UX should feature haptic elements like hover effects, fade-ins, smooth scroll, and subtle animations.

8. No form functionality is needed initially – the site is for informational purposes only.

9. Tone and design should be modern, professional, and accessible to all user types.

10. Components, sections, and images should be modular and reusable where possible.

11. Use functional components (arrow functions) with ES6+ syntax in all React code.

12. Component structure:
    - Each section (Hero, ProjectInfo, etc.) should be a separate file in the `components/` folder.
    - Layout and styling should be handled entirely with Tailwind CSS utility classes (no external CSS or CSS modules).
    - Images should be stored in an `assets/` folder and imported into components.

13. Tailwind conventions:
    - Follow mobile-first design: default styles for small screens, use `md:`, `lg:` etc for breakpoints.
    - Use Tailwind utilities for spacing, grid/flex, color, typography, transitions, etc.
    - Do not use inline styles (`style={{...}}`) – always use Tailwind classes.

14. Animation and haptics:
    - Use Tailwind's `transition`, `duration`, `ease`, `hover:` and `opacity-` for smooth interactions.
    - For more complex animations, you may use `framer-motion`, but keep it lightweight and minimal.

15. File and component naming: use PascalCase (e.g., `HeroSection.jsx`, `ProjectInfo.jsx`).

16. Use props to make components reusable, such as `<ImageSlider images={...} />`.

17. Store any copy that may change (like project info or headlines) in a `content.js` file or pass them via props.

18. Keep JSX clean and readable: break long lines, use semantic HTML tags (`<section>`, `<article>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`).

19. For icons, use [Lucide](https://lucide.dev/) – it works great with React and Tailwind.

20. Always test responsiveness in at least 3 viewports: mobile (<768px), tablet (768–1024px), and desktop (>1024px).
